panfrost: BOs anywhere in RAM, and no WARN when pages run out (ROADMAP 8.68)

Proposed, not flashed. Against build/linux-7.1-dp (7.1.0-zboot-wd-dp6).

The port's S9P_GEM_DMA32 keeps every Panfrost BO in ZONE_DMA (DMA32 is empty on
this phone: /proc/zoneinfo DMA 396037 pages managed, DMA32 0, Normal 504089).
GPU allocations failed with -ENOMEM (x0 = 0xfffffffffffffff4 in the WARN's
registers) while the Normal zone had room: 59 "panfrost_mmu.c:478
panfrost_mmu_map" WARNs in boot -2 of 2026-11-22 (41 ztsound, 16 ztmetro,
2 HwBinder), each ~60 ms of console output. Nothing Panfrost allocates is
scanned out (kmsro: the scanout buffers are s9p dumb buffers), and the G72's
MMU takes 40-bit physical addresses. To check before flashing: a client buffer
s9p would import for the plane path must still be refused above 4 GB
(s9p_decon_program_address writes a u32); today such an import already fails
unless the BO happens to be contiguous. ztmetro/FREEZE.md (2026-10-24) found
the same mechanism behind Superscan's freezes.

Apply: patch -p1 -d <kernel tree> < kernel/proposed/8.68-panfrost-no-dma32.patch

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_gem.c	2026-11-22 23:58:42.215814236 -0500
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_gem.c	2026-11-22 23:59:03.883222531 -0500
@@ -489,10 +489,19 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(shmem))
 		return ERR_CAST(shmem);
 
-	/* S9P_GEM_DMA32: below 4 GB, so KMS can scan this out directly */
-	mapping_set_gfp_mask(shmem->base.filp->f_mapping,
-			     (mapping_gfp_mask(shmem->base.filp->f_mapping)
-			      & ~__GFP_HIGHMEM) | __GFP_DMA32);
+	/*
+	 * S9P_GEM_DMA32 removed. It kept every BO below 4 GB "so KMS can scan
+	 * it out", but nothing Panfrost allocates is scanned out here: with
+	 * kmsro the shell's scanout buffers are s9p's own (dumb, DMA-contiguous,
+	 * made by the display device), and s9p's PRIME import of a shmem BO
+	 * fails anyway unless it is contiguous. On this phone ZONE_DMA32 is
+	 * empty and __GFP_DMA32 falls to ZONE_DMA, about 1.5 GB of the 3.5:
+	 * GPU memory ran out there with the Normal zone's 2 GB unused, and
+	 * every failure was a WARN in panfrost_mmu_map (59 in one boot of
+	 * 2026-11-22, from ztsound and ztmetro, ~60 ms of console each). The
+	 * Mali-G72's MMU takes 40-bit physical addresses (the dma mask is set
+	 * from MMU_FEATURES).
+	 */
 
 	bo = to_panfrost_bo(&shmem->base);
 	bo->noexec = !!(flags & PANFROST_BO_NOEXEC);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c	2026-11-22 23:58:42.215917884 -0500
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c	2026-11-22 23:59:03.883362523 -0500
@@ -475,8 +475,12 @@
 		prot |= IOMMU_NOEXEC;
 
 	sgt = drm_gem_shmem_get_pages_sgt(shmem);
-	if (WARN_ON(IS_ERR(sgt)))
+	if (IS_ERR(sgt)) {
+		/* out of memory (or a signal): the ioctl fails and Mesa copes;
+		 * not a kernel bug, so no WARN and its stack dump */
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(pfdev->base.dev, "BO map: no pages (%pe)\n", sgt);
 		return PTR_ERR(sgt);
+	}
 
 	ret = mmu_map_sg(pfdev, mapping->mmu, mapping->mmnode.start << PAGE_SHIFT,
 			 prot, sgt);
